Spec: Invoice Domain Model

Platform: Python 3

Purpose:
  Define immutable invoice values used by the sample service.

Structure:
  ./models.py: Domain model implementation.
  ./service.py: Consumer that creates invoices.
  ../../tests/test_service.py: Behavior coverage.

Owns:
  ./models.py
  ./models.sdd

Can modify:
  ./models.py
  ./models.sdd

Can read:
  ./service.py
  ../../tests/test_service.py

Must:
  Represent invoice lines as immutable values.
  Calculate line totals from quantity and unit price.
  Calculate invoice totals as the sum of line totals.
  Use Decimal for money arithmetic.
  Keep validation that depends on repository state outside the model.

Must not:
  Read files, environment variables, or network resources.
  Mutate invoice line collections after invoice creation.

Depends on:
  Python dataclasses
  Python decimal
  @invoice_demo.models.InvoiceLine
  @invoice_demo.models.Invoice

Scenario: invoice total is derived from line totals
  Given an invoice with multiple lines
  When @invoice_demo.models.Invoice.total is read
  Then it returns the sum of all @invoice_demo.models.InvoiceLine.total values

Example:
  model file: ./models.py
  test file: ../../tests/test_service.py
